          "level": 3,
          "area_of_effect": "1 spell",
          "duration": "—",
          "range": "varies",
          "type": "U",
          "subType": "-",
          "attack_table": "",
          "skillName": "",
          "description": "When this spell is cast, the first level spell that the caster begins to cast the next round will be \"channeled\" to another spell user of the Channeling realm. The \"channeled\" spell is transmitted to the other spell user when it would normally take effect, and must be used by the receiving spell user immediately (i.e., the receiving spell user is now treated as the caster of the spell). All normal restrictions apply to the transmitted spell. The caster of the Channels spell must be able to see the receiver of the spell or know exactly where he is (direction and distance, or specific location). The receiver must know exactly when the spell is coming (though he need not know exactly what spell is coming)."
        }
      },
